      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.455
      ],
      "seconds": 24.66,
      "text": "Galaxies spin too fast. At the speeds we measure, their outer stars should have been flung away billions of years ago. Something is holding them in that we cannot see, detect, or touch. The same accounting problem shows up in how the universe expands, and it is accelerating. Add it up and ordinary matter, everything we have ever observed, is about five percent of the total.",
